# Combat radio (HUD subtitles) and loading-screen tips.
# Story.radio_line(cue) picks one line of a cue at random; every line has a
# stable [ID:] so translations survive edits to the English text.
# The speaker name picks the portrait (game/ui/portrait.gd).

~ land_activate
Director Hale: Three generators, contractor. Turn them on, don't turn into one of them. [ID:RADIO_LAND_ACTIVATE_1]
Director Hale: Power's out on this rock. Fix that. Overtime is not authorised. [ID:RADIO_LAND_ACTIVATE_2]
=> END

~ land_defend
Director Hale: The uplink needs seventy-five seconds of uninterrupted transmission. Interrupt nothing. [ID:RADIO_LAND_DEFEND_1]
Director Hale: Plant yourself in the antenna zone. Think of it as a very aggressive meeting. [ID:RADIO_LAND_DEFEND_2]
=> END

~ land_rescue
Director Hale: One of our surveyors is still alive. Probably. Bring them back, they owe us a report. [ID:RADIO_LAND_RESCUE_1]
Director Hale: Survivor signal detected. Retrieval is billable, so let's do it right. [ID:RADIO_LAND_RESCUE_2]
=> END

~ land_holdout
Director Hale: The fort's yours until the boat gets there. Hold the courtyard, then get on board. [ID:RADIO_LAND_HOLDOUT_1]
Director Hale: Rescue boat is on its way. Keep the courtyard clear. And the pier. Especially the pier. [ID:RADIO_LAND_HOLDOUT_2]
=> END

~ land_hold_sequence
Director Hale: Survey points are marked, in order. Hold each one until the readings stick, then move. [ID:RADIO_LAND_HOLD_SEQUENCE_1]
Director Hale: One point at a time, contractor. The horde in between is not on the schedule. [ID:RADIO_LAND_HOLD_SEQUENCE_2]
=> END

~ land_fuel_run
Director Hale: The boat's running on fumes. Fuel cans on this rock, all marked. Bring them home. [ID:RADIO_LAND_FUEL_RUN_1]
Director Hale: Fuel run, contractor. No fuel, no ride home. I'd hate to bill you for the swim. [ID:RADIO_LAND_FUEL_RUN_2]
=> END

~ land_nests
Director Hale: Three nests on this rock, feeding the horde. Burn them out, in whatever order you like. [ID:RADIO_LAND_NESTS_1]
Director Hale: Nest removal, contractor. Every one you leave standing keeps making more of them. [ID:RADIO_LAND_NESTS_2]
=> END

~ land_intel_search
Director Hale: Our last survey team left their notes on this rock. Five places to look, three worth finding. The clock is running. [ID:RADIO_LAND_INTEL_SEARCH_1]
Director Hale: Intel recovery, contractor. Search fast, transmit what you find, and don't read it. [ID:RADIO_LAND_INTEL_SEARCH_2]
=> END

~ land_signals
Director Hale: The signal beacons on this rock are dark. Find their fuel, light them in order, and mind the queue that forms. [ID:RADIO_LAND_SIGNALS_1]
Director Hale: Beacon duty, contractor. One fire at a time, each one shows you the next. [ID:RADIO_LAND_SIGNALS_2]
=> END

~ land_boss
Director Hale: Thermal readings on the volcano are... large. Do the job, then leave before it notices. [ID:RADIO_LAND_BOSS_1]
=> END

~ generator
Director Hale: Generator online. Accounting thanks you. [ID:RADIO_GENERATOR_1]
Director Hale: That's one. The other two won't switch themselves on. [ID:RADIO_GENERATOR_2]
Director Hale: Power restored. Try not to stand in it. [ID:RADIO_GENERATOR_3]
=> END

~ hold_point
Director Hale: Point secured. Next one's marked. Don't stop to admire it. [ID:RADIO_HOLD_POINT_1]
Director Hale: Readings logged. Move to the next point before they log you. [ID:RADIO_HOLD_POINT_2]
=> END

~ hold_done
Director Hale: All points held. Survey complete. Get to the boat. [ID:RADIO_HOLD_DONE_1]
Director Hale: That's the last point. Now the hard part: leaving. [ID:RADIO_HOLD_DONE_2]
=> END

~ fuel_pickup
Director Hale: That's a full can. They heard you lift it. Walk faster. [ID:RADIO_FUEL_PICKUP_1]
Director Hale: Got it? Good. Hands full means no shooting. Put it down if you must, not for long. [ID:RADIO_FUEL_PICKUP_2]
=> END

~ fuel_delivered
Director Hale: Fuel's aboard. The next can won't carry itself. [ID:RADIO_FUEL_DELIVERED_1]
Director Hale: Delivered. Accounting wants a receipt. Go get another. [ID:RADIO_FUEL_DELIVERED_2]
=> END

~ fuel_done
Director Hale: Tanks are full. Get on the boat before the horde does. [ID:RADIO_FUEL_DONE_1]
Director Hale: That's the last can. Engine's warm. Climb aboard. [ID:RADIO_FUEL_DONE_2]
=> END

~ nest_destroyed
Director Hale: Nest down. Its friends are upset. Keep moving. [ID:RADIO_NEST_DESTROYED_1]
Director Hale: One less nursery. Pest control would charge double for that. [ID:RADIO_NEST_DESTROYED_2]
=> END

~ nests_done
Director Hale: Last nest's gone. The ones still walking didn't get the memo. Get to the boat. [ID:RADIO_NESTS_DONE_1]
Director Hale: Infestation cleared, mostly. Leave before the leftovers catch up. [ID:RADIO_NESTS_DONE_2]
=> END

~ intel_found
Director Hale: That's a file. Keep looking, the rest won't search themselves. [ID:RADIO_INTEL_FOUND_1]
Director Hale: Intel recovered. Legal says it's ours now. Next spot. [ID:RADIO_INTEL_FOUND_2]
=> END

~ intel_transmit
Director Hale: Get to the uplink and send what you have. Paper burns, signals don't. [ID:RADIO_INTEL_TRANSMIT_1]
Director Hale: Uplink's marked. Hold it while it sends. The horde hates good reception. [ID:RADIO_INTEL_TRANSMIT_2]
=> END

~ intel_done
Director Hale: Transmission received. Accounting is very excited. Get to the boat. [ID:RADIO_INTEL_DONE_1]
Director Hale: Data's in. You're now optional. Please extract anyway. [ID:RADIO_INTEL_DONE_2]
=> END

~ intel_none
Director Hale: Nothing to send? Then nothing to bill. Get to the boat. [ID:RADIO_INTEL_NONE_1]
=> END

~ signal_fuel
Director Hale: That's the fuel. Get it into the beacon before something gets it into you. [ID:RADIO_SIGNAL_FUEL_1]
Director Hale: Fuel acquired. No shooting with your hands full, so walk with purpose. [ID:RADIO_SIGNAL_FUEL_2]
=> END

~ signal_lit
Director Hale: Signal's burning. The next one's marked, a bit further in. They saw that too. [ID:RADIO_SIGNAL_LIT_1]
Director Hale: One fire lit. Follow the line, contractor, the next beacon is waiting. [ID:RADIO_SIGNAL_LIT_2]
=> END

~ signals_done
Director Hale: Every beacon's lit. Lovely view. Admire it from the boat. [ID:RADIO_SIGNALS_DONE_1]
Director Hale: Signals up, route marked. Now get yourself off this rock. [ID:RADIO_SIGNALS_DONE_2]
=> END

~ lighthouse_lit
Director Hale: The lighthouse is burning again. Every ship for miles can see it. So can they. Move. [ID:RADIO_LIGHTHOUSE_LIT_1]
=> END

~ objective_done
Director Hale: Objective complete. Get to the boat, the meter's running. [ID:RADIO_OBJECTIVE_DONE_1]
Director Hale: Good work. Now leave, quickly, with all your limbs. [ID:RADIO_OBJECTIVE_DONE_2]
=> END

~ objective_done_on_foot
Director Hale: Objective complete. Follow the path out, the next stretch won't clear itself. [ID:RADIO_OBJECTIVE_DONE_ON_FOOT_1]
Director Hale: Done here. Keep moving along the trail, no sightseeing. [ID:RADIO_OBJECTIVE_DONE_ON_FOOT_2]
=> END

~ survivor_found
Director Hale: Survivor located. Keep them breathing, the paperwork for the other outcome is awful. [ID:RADIO_SURVIVOR_FOUND_1]
Surveyor: You're from the company? Of course you are. Just get me out of here. [ID:RADIO_SURVIVOR_FOUND_2]
=> END

~ survivor_lost
Director Hale: Survivor lost. I'll file it under 'acceptable'. You won't. [ID:RADIO_SURVIVOR_LOST_1]
=> END

~ boss
Director Hale: That is the Behemoth. Company policy is: shoot it until it stops. [ID:RADIO_BOSS_1]
Director Hale: Large specimen inbound. Its rocks are not covered by your insurance. [ID:RADIO_BOSS_2]
=> END

~ boss_down
Director Hale: Behemoth down. Legal says we can now call this a 'successful outcome'. [ID:RADIO_BOSS_DOWN_1]
=> END

~ low_hp
Director Hale: Your vitals are trending towards 'former employee'. [ID:RADIO_LOW_HP_1]
Director Hale: Medical says you're leaking. Stop that. [ID:RADIO_LOW_HP_2]
=> END

~ screamer
Director Hale: That noise was a Screamer. Everything heard it. Everything. [ID:RADIO_SCREAMER_1]
=> END

~ cache
Director Hale: Supply cache cracked. Look, free stuff. Don't get used to it. [ID:RADIO_CACHE_1]
=> END

~ extract
Director Hale: On the boat. Nicely done, contractor. [ID:RADIO_EXTRACT_1]
=> END

# Loading-screen tips (one at random when the briefing has nothing specific).
~ tips
Director Hale: The breaker pushes them back. It is a door, not a weapon. Use it to make room. [ID:TIP_BREAKER]
Director Hale: Ammo is finite, contractor. Headshots are cheaper. [ID:TIP_HEADSHOTS]
Director Hale: Supply caches hide Intel files. Curiosity is billable. [ID:TIP_CACHES]
Director Hale: If they surround you, you stood still. Keep moving. [ID:TIP_MOVE]
Director Hale: Cards stack. Two of the same is rarely a mistake. [ID:TIP_CARDS]
Director Hale: Dying keeps your Intel. Extracting multiplies it. Do the maths. [ID:TIP_EXTRACT]
=> END
